  "id": "COMPOUND:22617 - PROTEIN:5837",
  "verbalization": "Certonardosterol E3 is implicated in the regulation of SN12K1 through a series of molecular interactions involving microtubule-associated proteins. The evidence suggests that Certonardosterol E3 acts as a target for multiple compounds, which in turn target these proteins, ultimately leading to the activation of SN12K1. The shared target of Microtubule-associated protein 1B across all three paths indicates a central role for this protein in the signaling cascade initiated by Certonardosterol E3. The presence of multiple downstream targets, including Cassialactone and Eugenitol, further supports a hierarchical pathway where Certonardosterol E3 influences the expression or activity of these proteins, which then interact with SN12K1. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Certonardosterol E3 may modulate SN12K1, possibly through the regulation of microtubule dynamics or other cellular processes. The consistency of the target relationships across the paths strengthens the hypothesis that Certonardosterol E3 and SN12K1 are linked via a well-defined, albeit indirect, molecular mechanism.",
